When using a VPN or proxy you should be concerned about what the VPN provider can see in your data, collect from it, and do to it. When you use a VPN, all data to and from your device goes through it.
For unencrypted services, it is possible for a VPN provider to see, collect, and modify (e.g., injecting ads into) the contents of your data. For encrypted data, it is still possible for a VPN to collect metadata about sites visited or actions taken.
