Flu usually comes on suddenly and sufferers will often experience muscle aches, chills, headaches, tiredness, a sore throat and a runny or stuffed nose, along with the cough. It feels worse than a heavy cold.
Fever, chills, muscle aches and headaches are rare. A Virus cough means coughing a lot for more than an hour, or three or more coughing fits or “episodes” in 24 hours.
You should get tested for Virus if you develop a new, continuous cough.
