Basically, an industrial robot is an electromechanical machine that can solve complex series of tasks without (or at least) human intervention.
Slip rings play a vital role in the robotics industry. Sometimes in robot applications, slip rings are also called “robot slip rings” or “robot rotating joints.”
Cylindrical robot 3.
How to use slip ring in robots Let us take a look at how slip ring technology is used in these robot applications.
• In Cartesian robots, slip ring technology is used to lift and move heavy objects or products in all directions. Automating this heavy labor can prevent the need for additional employees and save time.
• Cylindrical robots are used for assembly operations, spot welding, metal casting in foundries, and other cyclically coordinated mechanical handling tools. For this circulatory coordination, slip ring technology is used.
• With the help of slip ring technology, polar or spherical robots are used for machine tool processing and machine management (such as gas welding, arc welding, die casting, injection molding, painting and extrusion components).
• In industrial robots, slip ring technology is widely used to design printed circuit boards (PCBs) in a modular and compact design. With the help of slip ring technology, we can trigger and execute repetitive tasks.
• In the food and pharmaceutical industries, slip ring technology is used by robots to complete repetitive tasks. With just a few commands to the robot, we can perform multiple tasks that require more manpower.
There is no doubt that slip ring technology is in great demand and has broad prospects. If you have any questions about the apps we are discussing here, please let me know in the comments.
