Agricultural technology still has a long way to go, but it is catching up. Although the mechanical harvesting of citrus encountered obstacles when the HLB arrived, it has been rejuvenated today after a hurricane in the mid-2000s.
Autonomous robots use lidar vision to move in the woods, reducing the need for human operators. One person can operate four machines with one laptop in his or her pickup cab.
