Safety Guidelines What should I do to prevent a fire, or handle one if one occurs
- Always use standard electrical products, and do not connect multiple devices to a single wall socket.
※ In a fire, children and infants must leave the building immediately, and must not attempt to extinguish the fire even if they know how to use an extinguisher.
Do not connect multiple devices to a single outlet.
If an electrical device is not working properly, or has an unusual odor, shut it off immediately and contact a professional for an inspection.
If there is anything unusual occurring in relation to the electricity, report it to Korea Electric Power Corporation (123) or Korea Electrical Safety Corporation (1588-7500).
Inspect the internal parts of all switches and distribution boxes, and do not leave conductors and/or flammables nearby.
- Mix dish detergent and water in a 1:1 ratio, shake well to form bubbles, and apply a sufficient amount on the connecting parts using a brush or a sponge.
If you smell gas fr om damaged or loose valves or hoses, close the gas valve on the outside, open the windows to ventilate, and call a professional for a repair.
Sound the alarm to let others know about the fire, and evacuate immediately.
If possible, call 119 immediately.
Evacuate through a route with less flame and smoke.
Before opening a door, place your hand on the surface of the door to check whether it is hot. If the door is heated, do not open it: evacuate through a different route.
If you cannot see due to heavy smoke, hold on to the walls to evacuate.
When evacuating through an emergency exit, always close the door after you to prevent flame and smoke fr om expanding.
“There is a fire on the second floor of ○○ Villa next to ○○ elementary school in Sindang-dong, Jung-gu, Seoul.” Leave your phone number.
While it is possible to track down the location and phone number of a person who calls 119, you should still give this information correctly for a faster dispatch.
Do not hang up until your report is received by the fire station.
- Emergency reports can also be made with a suspended cell phone or a cell phone that is not connected to the service.
- If you have water, sprinkle it on flammable objects, partitions and curtains to delay the fire’s spread.
- If anyone is missing, report how many are missing and where you saw them last to a fire officer immediately.
If you have been injured by a fire, contact your insurance company to receive benefits.
- Commercial law and standard insurance policies stipulate that one must notify his/her insurance company of any accident without delay. As such, the insurance company will not pay for damages that are extended due to a delay in giving notification.
Report to the tax office about the fire for tax support, including a deferment of collection. - It is possible to receive a deduction for your loss fr om the disaster.
- You can also receive a prompt return of VAT.
- You can receive a local tax exemption.
