Gas boilers must always be installed in a well-ventilated place.
Gas pipes shall be colored and installed properly in a well-ventilated place.
Apply an ample amount of soapy water (1:1 ratio of dish detergent and water) on a spot that is likely to have a leak.
Open up the windows and ventilate the room before use.
While cooking, be careful not to lose the flame due to the wind or a boil over.
·Gas safety guidelines for each season
- If hot weather continues, install a shade over the LPG tank.
- When there is a risk of a flood, LPG users should close the tank valve and move the tank to a safe place such as a rooftop.
- If you find damage, contact the installer or manufacturer for a repair. Contact information can usually be found on the gas boiler.
- If the cold weather is causing difficulties in using LPG, cover up the tank with a thick cloth. Do not bring fire, or pour hot water over the LPG tank.
Do not ignite a flame (including heaters). Do not use a fan, as it requires the ignition of a spark to start.
Open the windows and move the victim to a well-ventilated room.
If the victim has something inside his/her mouth, remove it immediately.
If the victim stops breathing, give him/her mouth-to-mouth.
Take the victim to a hospital where a high-pressure oxygen respirator is available.
Cool down the affected skin using clean water and go to the hospital immediately.
Do not pop any blisters. Apply a piece of gauze to the wound, and seek proper treatment immediately.
