And if there's carnival, there's a lot of frevo on the streets of Recife and Olinda, the Pernambuco cities that put together some of the most disputed parties of the Brazilian carnival, attracting thousands of revelers from all over Brazil and abroad. In Olinda, Homem da Meia Noite is already rehearsing his steps with Mulher do Meio Dia, so that together they can pull dozens of other giant puppets along the slopes of the city's historic center.
After all, we are talking about the most democratic party in the world! Whether in Olinda or Recife, it's certain that a lot of frevo and maracatu will roll through the streets of both cities, with incredible local dancers rocking the choreography, adorned by the color of their clothes and umbrellas.
