It is difficult to find a Brazilian who does not know how to prepare a caipirinha, and it is almost impossible to find someone who does not know that the basic ingredients of this drink are cachaça, lemon, sugar and ice. But do you know how the caipirinha was born?
Nor would I consider it impossible to mix the two theses, that is, the creation of caipirinha to be served at important events for sugarcane producers, based on a recipe for a home remedy. And why not?
Like a good bar conversation, we talked and talked and we didn't come to any conclusion about the inventor of the caipirinha. So, how about we simply take a lemon cut into segments, add sugar, crush the segments, add some ice cubes and, finally, add a shot of cachaça and drink this wonder that is part of the Brazilian essence?
