Two months ago we addressed the issue of "terroir" in this space, but we decided to return to the topic in this issue because of the large number of questions that reached our editorial office. By the way, I would like to take this opportunity to confirm that if you have any questions or suggestions about the universe of wines, you can write to us (editorial@suoviaggio.com.br) that we will address the issue in the future to try to clarify as much as we can.
Will the wines be of the same quality or could they be of different qualities due to the terroir?
As we saw in the first column on terroir, this terminology is very broad, considering not only the soil and subsoil, but also including other characteristics such as altitude, relief, environment and climate, forming a set of parameters that contribute to the result of the wine. Therefore, if we consider two geographical areas that are very different from each other, even using the same techniques, the wines at the end of the process will be different.
