The dynamic and cosmopolitan city that became a reference in culture and gastronomy celebrates 468 years of life
And for those who still dare to say that São Paulo is an ugly city, here's an invitation to appreciate the city's skyline with eyes devoid of prejudice. It is true that São Paulo does not have the sea, but it has countless other attributes.
Not even the biggest critic of the city will be able to question the cultural vein that this city has, with its hundreds of theaters, cinemas, concert halls and museums, providing a cultural agenda so vast and rich that the mission of following everything that happens in the city it became impossible. I would like to see greater appreciation of the spaces that portray the history of São Paulo, but I am confident that we will improve in this regard as well.
The city offers us typical cuisine restaurants from the most different regions of the world, providing us with a true journey around the world through gastronomy. If you come from São Paulo, you are invited to experience the city as a tourist; if you are not from São Paulo, you are invited to visit and let yourself be enchanted by this incredible city!
